  "result": "I added `chunk<T>(items, size)` in `src/core/chunk.ts` and committed it as `2ccec06`. The three tests in `test/core/chunk.test.ts` pass, and `tsc --noEmit` and `biome check` are clean. I did not run the full `npm run gate` or `npm run lint`, which also runs `scripts/boundaries.ts`.\n\n- **Behaviour:** it returns the groups in order, and the last group is shorter if the list doesn't divide evenly. An empty list gives `[]`.\n- **Rejected sizes:** it throws a `RangeError` for a size below 1. It also rejects non-integers and `NaN`, which you didn't ask for, because a size like 1.5 would otherwise produce odd groups.\n- **Reuse:** `src/core` only contains type definitions, and I found no existing chunking helper in `src/`. So there was nothing to reuse, and the function uses only built-ins.\n- **Tests:** the tests cover a short last group, empty input, a size larger than the list, and the rejected sizes. I put them in a new `test/core/` directory.",
